@Make(Article)
@Use(Bibliography = "refs.bib")
@Device(LPT)

@Begin(TitlePage)
@Begin(Center)
@B(A Simple Scribe Document)

John Doe
Computer Science Department
January 1, 1980
@End(Center)
@End(TitlePage)

@Section(Introduction)
This is a simple example of a Scribe document. Scribe is a markup
language and document preparation system developed in the 1970s
at Carnegie Mellon University.

@Section(Features)
Scribe provides several features:
@Begin(Itemize)
@Item{Document structure commands}
@Item{Cross-references and citations}
@Item{Automatic numbering and formatting}
@End(Itemize)

@Section(Conclusion)
Scribe was influential in the development of later markup
languages like LaTeX.
